#!/bin/rc
# /home/profile/start.rc — kitty's, run when they log in, after the
# system's /profile/start.rc (docs/packages.md). Theirs to change. Plan 9's
# counterpart is `$home/lib/profile`, which init runs the same way
# (`plan9/sys/src/cmd/init.c:178`).

# kitty's services (docs/packages.md): each named in /home/profile/service
# without a leading `!`, started at login
if(test -r /home/profile/service)
	for(s in `{sed '/^[!#]/d' /home/profile/service})
		service start -u $s

# the window manager, where the host has one (docs/emca.md, Boot and the
# session): the page's serves its files on #9/1, and emca's IPNX half is a
# service, started at login as Plan 9's profile starts rio on a terminal.
# Which host this is, is $terminal, as Plan 9's termrc asks it (`~
# $terminal *vx32*`, termrc:48) — a terminal's #9/1 is its host's commands
# (docs/saranos.md), and the page's console has no #9/1 — and where there
# is none, nothing to report: init prints the status a profile ends with
# (`init.c:164`), and a test that failed is one
if(~ $terminal *hosts/web* && test -e '#9/1')
	service start -s emca
if not
	status=''
